From 571eeed0768f8cacd109284f17593a3d1048ad30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 05:55:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ground battle (release 2): run styles, each man his own
 runner (behind the "runs" trial)

Brian, 23 Nov: "multiple animations of the players running so not all players
are running exactly the same at the same time". The soldier files now carry
three more runs and three more advances (run_b/c/d, advance_b/c/d: other
runners' motion capture, the soldiers thread's run_styles.py), each naming the
clip it is a style of (style_of). LandMen reads that (Soldier::Styles); with
Crowd::SetRunStyles on, each man's gait plays his own one of the four by his
seed (the same runner running or advancing), at his speed over the clip's own,
so the long striders step slower than the short ones and no two keep step. Far
men banked in poses show the base clip's poses. Off unless set; the scene sets
it on the "runs" trial, "-TheaterLandNoRunStyles" off.

land_show_test: LAND_SHOW_RUN_STYLES=1 plays it; the four runners each on at
least a tenth of the running, and none but the file's own with it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz3YSqBqHKxvTEycWyM
